    "note": "Version read: Introduced (date field 0000-00-00). Borderline gun_policy: the bill only changes public-records exemptions for gun licensing and transfer records, but those records are part of the firearms licensing system, so marked true. Sec. 1 amends RCW 42.56.240(4); the bill adds the words in (a) and new (b) and (c)."
  },
  "operative_text": "Sec. 1 (RCW 42.56.240): (4)(a) License applications, licenses, notices of license denials, and any documents associated with a license or license application, including proof of completion of a certified concealed carry firearms safety training program, under RCW 9.41.070, except that copies of license applications or information on the applications may be released to law enforcement or corrections agencies or to persons and entities as authorized under RCW 9.41.815;\nSec. 1 (RCW 42.56.240): (b) Permit applications, permits, notices of permit denials, and any documents associated with a permit or permit application, including a certificate of completion of a certified firearms safety training program, under RCW 9.41.121, except that copies of permit applications or information on the applications may be released to law enforcement or corrections agencies or to persons and entities as authorized under RCW 9.41.815; and\nSec. 1 (RCW 42.56.240): (c) Applications for the purchase or transfer of a firearm, firearm transfer records, notices of application denials, and any documents associated with an application for the purchase or transfer of a firearm, under chapter 9.41 RCW, except that firearm transfer records and copies of applications for the purchase or transfer of a firearm or information on the applications may be released to law enforcement or corrections agencies or to persons and entities as authorized under RCW 9.41.815;"
}